From 74f2dee5fab9592234b7823df36b4b84bf780125 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: telegdyd <telegdyd93@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 06:49:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] jasmine-j0041: why OSM does not move the clock: LLM/CC off,
 sequencer load (osmseq=1)

Round j40: OSM enabled, LUT read back correct, TZ sequencer writes taken,
desired index stepped 0..3, but the Gold PLL stayed at L 0x20, the RCG on
GPLL0 (index 0's source), pstate 0, CPRh corner 0 (the sdm660-mainline
OSM driver's SDM660 tester saw the same). Phase 2 now logs the sequencer
PC, the OSM cycle counter and the perf-state interrupt status, and when
the clock did not follow (A) it tries:
 B: OSM following only the software request (LLM_INTF_DCVS_DISABLE 3,
    SPM_CC_DCVS_DISABLE 1), stepped again;
 C (osmseq=1): OSM off, the sequencer loaded as msm-4.4 clk-cpu-osm.c
    does without TZ (qcom,osm-no-tz: program, branch table, PLL L / post
    div, APM, GFMUX, ITM, APM corner pointers), every word through TZ IO
    writes; MEM-ACC levels all get the MEM-ACC registers' current value
    (msm8998's APCS 0x179d1368/6c/70; SDM660's values are TZ's), so its
    switches change nothing; then enabled at index 0 and stepped again.
Still capped by osmmax= (default 1747200 kHz, below the APM corner).

The sequencer program is copied from msm-4.4 clk-cpu-osm.c (The Linux
Foundation, GPL-2.0; the user's OK of 2026-10-22).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 osfmk/arm64/sweet_osm.c | 252 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 222 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)

